{
    "attributes": {
        "action": "Fund the creation of specialist autistic and PDA schools",
        "additional_details": "We believe children who experience severe anxiety, sensory difficulties and demand avoidance need education that adapts to them, including:\r\n1.\tSmall, sensory-friendly settings\r\n2.\tAutism and PDA-trained staff\r\n3.\tFlexible attendance and reduced demands\r\n4.\tGreater choice and individualised learning\r\nChildren should not have to reach crisis point or lose years of education before receiving appropriate support. Every child deserves an education that works for them and enables them to reach their potential.",
        "background": "We want the Government to fund the creation of new flexible specialist schools for autistic children, particularly those with a Pathological Demand Avoidance (PDA) profile, who cannot access mainstream or traditional special schools.",
